<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uzbeks</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Uzbek</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Uzbeks are a Turkic people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> whose name derives from the nomadic confederation that formed in the fifteenth century. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-shaybani">Muhammad Shaybani</a> they conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurids</a> around 1500, ending Timurid rule there and driving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> south. They became persistent rivals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>, raiding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> reconquered it in 1598.</p></div>
